1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
AERO Guard — Intelligent Anomaly Detection for Automatic Weather Stations.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Automatic Weather Stations support forecasting, agriculture, aviation, disaster management, and climate monitoring. Faulty readings can put these decisions at risk.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:50,000
AERO Guard monitors temperature, atmospheric pressure, and relative humidity together. It learns normal temporal and seasonal patterns using a multivariate LSTM autoencoder.

4
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The prototype generates realistic AWS data and injects spikes, frozen values, sensor drift, and communication loss for repeatable evaluation.

5
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:28,000
The model learns normal behavior and uses reconstruction error to identify unusual time windows.

6
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:46,000
A real-time FastAPI service returns an anomaly score, severity, confidence, and probable root cause for every incoming observation.

7
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The Streamlit dashboard gives operators a clear view of readings, alerts, and sensor health.

8
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Explainable diagnostics help identify spikes, frozen sensors, abrupt drift, and communication problems.

9
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:31,000
A compact quantized TensorFlow Lite model can run near the sensor on an ESP32, enabling low-power edge detection.

10
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:46,000
We evaluate detection using injected anomalies and metrics such as precision, recall, F1 score, false alarm rate, and latency.

11
00:02:46,000 --> 00:03:00,000
AERO Guard is a practical step toward a self-aware and self-healing weather observation network. It makes weather observations trustworthy.
